cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this panel, its QC gates or the analysis code, please cite this repository."
title: "Physical-Recapture Proxy Selection: a pre-registered study of AI-image detector degradation under screen photography"
authors:
  - family-names: "TODO-family-name"
    given-names: "TODO-given-name"
    affiliation: "TODO-affiliation"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/OWNER/proxy-selection-research"
license: MIT
version: "0.5.0"
date-released: "2026-11-02"
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered, attempt-logged study of how AI-image detectors degrade when
  their inputs are photographed off a screen. 998 physical frames, 6 frozen
  detectors, 4 digital degradation families, same-source digital-to-physical
  pairing (899 sources / 17,994 pairs), and a pre-registered selection-loss
  replay (EXAM05, negative at b=40).
keywords:
  - AI-image detection
  - physical recapture
  - screen photography
  - benchmark validity
  - pre-registration
